Hi all,

Recently I changed computer and freshly installed TMB, but am getting an ambiguous 'compilation failed' error. I did some googling and most people get this when rtools isn't installed, however I have checked that Rtools is available. The weird thing is when I install some github repos with TMB compiled code, it compiles fine. So I am thinking it is a path issue or something. Any tips would be appreciated.

#If you install package from source you must have Rtools right?
install.packages("TMB",type="source")
library(TMB)
runExample(all=TRUE) ## get the error here
Building example ar1xar1
Error in compile(paste0(name, ".cpp"), ...) : Compilation failed
Timing stopped at: 0.02 0 0.02
sessionInfo()
R version 4.0.2 (2020-06-22)
Platform: x86_64-w64-mingw32/x64 (64-bit)
Running under: Windows 10 x64 (build 18363)

Matrix products: default

locale:
[1] LC_COLLATE=English_New Zealand.1252  LC_CTYPE=English_New Zealand.1252
[3] LC_MONETARY=English_New Zealand.1252 LC_NUMERIC=C
[5] LC_TIME=English_New Zealand.1252

attached base packages:
[1] stats     graphics  grDevices utils     datasets  methods   base

other attached packages:
[1] TMB_1.7.22

loaded via a namespace (and not attached):
[1] compiler_4.0.2  Matrix_1.3-4    tools_4.0.2     grid_4.0.2      lattice_0.20-41
library(pkgbuild)
has_rtools()
[1] TRUE
Regards,
C

